fund-js/03-functions-in-depth/01-pipe.solution:
export function pipe(...fns) {
  return (...args) => {
    if (fns.length === 0) return args[0];
    let value = fns[0](...args);
    for (const fn of fns.slice(1)) value = fn(value);
    return value;
  };
}

fund-js/03-functions-in-depth/01-pipe.explanation:
Call the first function with the spread arguments, then fold the rest over the running value:

```js
export function pipe(...fns) {
  return (...args) => {
    if (fns.length === 0) return args[0];
    let value = fns[0](...args);
    for (const fn of fns.slice(1)) value = fn(value);
    return value;
  };
}
```

`fns.reduce((v, fn) => fn(v), args[0])` is shorter but fails the "every argument" test: the first function would see only one argument.

