export function memoize(fn) {
  // TODO: a cache that survives between calls
}

fund-js/03-functions-in-depth/02-memoize.solution:
export function memoize(fn) {
  const cache = new Map();
  return (arg) => {
    if (!cache.has(arg)) cache.set(arg, fn(arg));
    return cache.get(arg);
  };
}

fund-js/03-functions-in-depth/02-memoize.explanation:
A `Map` in the closure, checked with `has` (not with the stored value):

```js
export function memoize(fn) {
  const cache = new Map();
  return (arg) => {
    if (!cache.has(arg)) cache.set(arg, fn(arg));
    return cache.get(arg);
  };
}
```

A plain object cache fails the `0` / `'0'` test (keys become strings), and `if (cache.get(arg) === undefined)` fails the boundary test.
